#. Tag: title
#: commands-palettes.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Palettes</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section describes &krita;'s palettes. The palettes are usually found at "
"the right hand side of &krita;'s main window. There are three palettes which "
"help you in customizing your images:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-palettes.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Control box</guilabel> palette"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Control box</guilabel> contains three tabs. You can get an "
"overview of the image, view a color histogram, and modify options for the "
"current tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Resumit"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Overview</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Overview</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Overview</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab offers you two settings. With the spinbox, slider, and "
"<guibutton>1:1</guibutton> button at the bottom, you can set the zoom level "
"for the document. The <guilabel>Exposure</guilabel> slider and textbox can "
"be used to choose the exposure level for OpenEXR images. Furthermore, the "
"<guilabel>X</guilabel> and <guilabel>Y</guilabel> labels indicate the "
"current pointer position, with (0,0) being the top left corner of the canvas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Histogram"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Histogram</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Histogram</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Histogram</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab displays a color histogram showing the distribution of colors over "
"the image. The histogram is split up in red, green and blue levels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tool"
msgstr "Esplech"

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actually, there is no tab named like this, since the tab name changes to "
"reflect the name of the currently selected tool. This tab shows the "
"customization options available for the tools that have them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Brush"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Brush</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Brush</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Brush</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three options available on this tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Opacity</guilabel> slider and spin box are used to set the "
"opacity when drawing (opacity is the opposite of transparency, i.e. 100% "
"opaque is 0% transparent, and vice versa)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Mode</guilabel> drop down box, you can choose a drawing "
"mode. This changes the actual effect that results from drawing on the image "
"(for example, only changing the saturation or lightness)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the <guilabel>Paint direct</guilabel> option, you can determine whether "
"you want to paint directly on the current layer, or on a temporary layer "
"which is then composited onto the actual layer. This makes a difference "
"especially when using relative low opacity values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line"
msgstr "Linha"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Line</guilabel></"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Line</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Line</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-brush\">Brush</link> "
"for the description of <guilabel>Opacity</guilabel> and <guilabel>Mode</"
"guilabel>. The <guilabel>?</guilabel> button shows a tip about the usage of "
"modifier keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rectangle"
msgstr "Rectangle"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Rectangle</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Tool tab for <guilabel>Rectangle</guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Tool tab for <guilabel>Rectangle</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-brush\">Brush</link> "
"for a description of <guilabel>Opacity</guilabel> and <guilabel>Mode</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Fill</guilabel> drop down box is used to specify whether the "
"inside of the rectangle should be filled. You can choose between three fill "
"options: the current foreground color, background color or pattern is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bezier"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-brush\">Brush</link> "
"for the description of <guilabel>Mode</guilabel> and <guilabel>Opacity</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ellipse"
msgstr "Ellipsa"

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:161 commands-palettes.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same options as for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-"
"rectangle\">Rectangle</link> are available here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Polygon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Polyline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same options as for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-"
"line\">Line</link> are available here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Star"
msgstr "Estèla"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Star</guilabel></"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Star</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Star</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The options for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-rectangle"
"\">Rectangle</link> are available here, as well as two options specific to "
"this tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Vertices</guilabel> drop down box is used to set the amount of "
"vertices (points) in the star."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Ratio</guilabel> setting defines the shape of the star. A "
"ratio of 0% will create a star with no inner area (when drawing the star, "
"the two lines that make up a star point, overlap). Increasing the ratio will "
"slowly make the star more outlined (the two lines are <quote>pulled apart</"
"quote>). A star with a ratio of 100% is a regular polygon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Duplicate"
msgstr "Duplicar"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Duplicate</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Duplicate</"
"guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Duplicate</guilabel></"
"para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same options as for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-"
"line\">Line</link> are available here. In addition, there are three other "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the <guilabel>Healing</guilabel> and <guilabel>Healing radius</"
"guilabel> options, you can specify that the duplication should not copy the "
"colors, but only the <quote>structure</quote> of the source area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you enable the <guilabel>Correct the perspective</guilabel> option, the "
"duplicate tool will follow your perspective grid."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Paint with Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Paint with "
"Filters</guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Paint with Filters</"
"guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Paint with Filters</"
"guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the filter, you can set different options here. The options you "
"can set are the same as those available in the <quote>normal</quote> "
"settings dialog for the chosen filter. See the <link linkend=\"commands-"
"dialogs-filters\">Filters section in the Dialogs chapter</link> for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "Transform"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Transform</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Transform</"
"guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Transform</guilabel></"
"para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose which transformation algorithm to use in the "
"<guilabel>Filter</guilabel> drop down box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crop"
msgstr "Rosegar"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Crop</guilabel></"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Crop</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Crop</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the corner coordinates of the area that should remain with the four spin "
"boxes <guilabel>X</guilabel>, <guilabel>Y</guilabel>, <guilabel>Width</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Height</guilabel>. You can also fill in "
"<guilabel>Ratio</guilabel> to determine the Y/X ratio. Check one of the "
"checkboxes to have the respective value remain constant while changing the "
"size of the area. The drop down box can be used to select whether the entire "
"image or only the current layer should be cropped. Clicking the "
"<guibutton>Crop</guibutton> button has the same effect as double-clicking "
"outside the area in the image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contiguous Fill"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</"
"guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</"
"guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:330 commands-palettes.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same options as for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-"
"brush\">Brush</link> are available here, as are a couple of other options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The setting in the <guilabel>Threshold</guilabel> slider and spin box "
"determines how near the color of a point should be to the color of the "
"starting point of the fill, in order for the fill to spread out over the "
"former point. A higher threshold will therefore fill areas that have less "
"similar colors, a lower threshold limits the spread."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you check the <guilabel>Fill entire selection</guilabel> checkbox, the "
"entire selection will be filled instead of only the neighboring area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking the <guilabel>Limit to current layer</guilabel> checkbox changes "
"the behavior of the fill: the extent to which the fill is done, is "
"determined from the current layer only instead of the entire image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By checking the <guilabel>Use pattern</guilabel> checkbox you can choose to "
"fill with the currently selected pattern instead of with the foreground "
"color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gradient"
msgstr "Degradat"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Gradient</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Gradient</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Gradient</guilabel></"
"para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Shape</guilabel> drop down box can be used to select the "
"gradient type: <guilabel>Linear</guilabel>, <guilabel>Bi-Linear</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Radial</guilabel>, <guilabel>Square</guilabel>, <guilabel>Conical</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Conical Symmetric</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Repeat</guilabel> option determines whether the gradient is "
"repeated if it does not fill the entire image. With <guilabel>None</"
"guilabel>, the colors on the ends of the gradient are used to fill the "
"remaining space. With <guilabel>Forwards</guilabel>, the gradient is "
"normally repeated (connecting the back end of one occurrence with the front "
"end of the next). With <guilabel>Alternating</guilabel>, the gradient is "
"repeated with every second occurrence being drawn from back to front "
"(linking front to front and back to back)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check the <guilabel>Reverse</guilabel> checkbox to have the gradient drawn "
"reversed (from back to front)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The final setting is <guilabel>Anti-alias threshold</guilabel>, which "
"determines how smooth the gradient will become."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text"
msgstr "Tèxt"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Text</guilabel></"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Text</guilabel></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Text</guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same options as for <link linkend=\"commands-palettes-controlbox-tool-"
"brush\">Brush</link> are available here. Furthermore there is an option "
"<guilabel>Font</guilabel>, which shows the font that will be used for the "
"text. Click the <guibutton>...</guibutton> button to change the font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color Picker"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Color Picker</"
"guilabel></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Color Picker</"
"guilabel></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<para>The <guilabel>Tool</guilabel> tab for <guilabel>Color Picker</"
"guilabel></para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first option is a dropdown box in which you can choose which layer to "
"pick the color from. If you choose a specific layer, the color of the point "
"in that layer will be retrieved. With <guilabel>Sample All Visible Layers</"
"guilabel>, the topmost visible layer which is not transparent at that point "
"is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Update current color</guilabel> checkbox is checked, then "
"the current foreground color (when clicking with the &LMB;) or background "
"color (when clicking with the &RMB;) is set to the picked color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checkbox <guilabel>Add to palette</guilabel> and the accompanying "
"dropdown box determine whether the picked color should be added to an "
"existing palette. Check the checkbox, and choose the desired palette from "
"the list, if you want to do so."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checkbox <guilabel>Show colors as percentages</guilabel> switches the "
"range of color values displayed from the <quote>normal</quote> range (e.g. 0 "
"to 255) to a scaled value between 0% and 100%."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the <guilabel>Sample radius</guilabel> option, you can choose the area "
"size to use when picking the color. A radius of one just picks one pixel, "
"larger radii will make the picker average over the colors of the circle-"
"shaped area with the chosen radius that is centered around the chosen pixel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-palettes.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Select</guilabel> tools"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
