#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Distance</guilabel> option determines the maximal distance at "
"which boundaries to attach to, are searched for. The <guibutton>To "
"Selection</guibutton> button has the same effect as double-clicking the "
"&LMB;: the selection is finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-palettes.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> palette"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this palette you can choose the foreground and background colors that "
"should be used for painting. You can choose these in five different ways. "
"Each of these has its own tab on this palette."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose which color to set by clicking the corresponding buttons at "
"the top left. The topmost color is the foreground color, the bottom one is "
"the background color. You can click the double-headed arrow to swap the "
"colors: foreground color becomes background color and vice versa. You can "
"reset the colors to the default (foreground black, background white) by "
"clicking the small black/white icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>HSV</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>HSV</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>HSV</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>HSV</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:578
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select a color via the Hue / Saturation / Value system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The hue determines the major color and starts at red with 0, then increases "
"along the color spectrum (that is, along the <quote>line</quote> yellow, "
"green, blue, violet) to a maximum of 359. This is represented in the circle "
"on the tab as the angle component (starting at the top, rotate along the "
"circle in clockwise direction to increase the hue)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The saturation determines the pureness of the color. A saturation of 255 "
"yields the pure color, while a saturation of 0 yields a gray. This is the "
"radius component of the color circle on the tab: the center corresponds to "
"no saturation, the circle boundary corresponds to fully saturated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value determines the lightness of the color. This darkens or lightens "
"the color, as can be set using the vertical slider on the tab. A value of 0 "
"gives black, a value of 255 gives the pure color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>RGB</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>RGB</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>RGB</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>RGB</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, colors can be selected using their Red / Green / Blue "
"components."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set red, green and blue components on a scale of 0 to 255. At 0 that "
"color component is absent, at 255 it is used at maximum intensity. The "
"sliders will change color to give you a hint about which color you will "
"produce by altering the corresponding value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gray"
msgstr "Escala de grises"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Gray</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Gray</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Gray</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can choose a gray value (indicated with a K for Key, the "
"usual designation for black)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The gray value can be chosen on a scale from 0 (pure white) to 255 (pure "
"black)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Palettes</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Palettes</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Palettes</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Palettes</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this tab, you can select a color from one of several predefined color "
"palettes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:664
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose which color palette to pick from in the drop down box at the "
"top."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid "Watercolors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Watercolors</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Watercolors</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Watercolors</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab offers you a selection of watercolors for painting with <quote>wet "
"paint</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set two options to modify the painting behaviour: <guilabel>Paint "
"strength</guilabel> influences how much paint you will apply to the canvas, "
"and <guilabel>Wetness</guilabel> determines how wet the paint is when it is "
"applied. You can dry the paint later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: commands-palettes.docbook:697
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Layers</guilabel> palette"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid "This palette offers two tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: commands-palettes.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid "Layers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: commands-palettes.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Layers</guilabel> tab</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: commands-palettes.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Layers</guilabel> tab</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Layers</guilabel> tab</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid "This tab offers you access to various operations on layers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the top left, you can select what blending mode should be used for the "
"selected layer. These are the same possibilities as you can choose from for "
"drawing modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The slider/textbox at the top right determines the opacity of the selected "
"layer. 0% opacity corresponds to 100% transparency, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The list shows all layers and their names, and offers various controls for "
"each layer. The eye icon toggles whether the layer is visible or not. The "
"link icon is used to link layers together. The lock icon determines if the "
"layer is locked or not. Locked layers cannot be edited."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the layer list, there are some other controls. You can create a new "
"layer, move the current layer up or down, show the layer's properties and "
"delete it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: commands-palettes.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are some more handy tricks you can do with the mouse within the list. "
"Right-click on the layer list and select <guilabel>New Folder</guilabel> to "
"create a new layer folder, which you can use to group layers in. You can "
"also drag and drop layers to change their order. To do so, click on the "
"bottom part of the list item representing the layer, drag the mouse, and "
"release the mouse button at the desired position. If you click at the top "
"part of the list item instead, you will get a text field so that you can "
"rename the layer."
msgstr ""

